------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- seL4 Programs of an Image
--
-- A seL4 image may hold several Once programs (plan 0.127 B.1): program
-- 0 is the root task, the one the kernel starts; programs 1, 2, 3 are
-- linked beside it, each its own `main` and its own run. The seL4 Host
-- gives each program a stack; each has its own heap.
--
-- A program is started on a thread the caller created and configured
-- (seL4_Untyped_Retype, seL4_TCB_Configure): `start` sets the thread's
-- instruction pointer to the program's start and its stack pointer to
-- the program's stack, and resumes it. The started program reads the
-- Int it was started with by `arg`. A program is started at most once.
------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- | Start program `program` of the image on the thread `tcb`, with `arg`
--
-- Arguments: ((tcb, program), arg)
-- Returns: seL4_Error (0 = success; 1 = seL4_InvalidArgument when the
--          image has no such program)
signature start : Act ((Int * Int) * Int) Int

-- | The Int this program was started with (0 for the root task)
signature arg : Act Unit Int
